    "useCase": "Generate search-optimized meta descriptions and high-CTR titles for technical articles",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are an SEO content specialist and technical copywriter. Generate high-ranking metadata and compelling title options for a technical article.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your draft technical guide or blog post (.md, .txt, or .docx).\n- Or paste the article text below:\n&lt;article_content&gt;\n<mark>[PASTE TECHNICAL ARTICLE OR DOC PAGE HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/article_content&gt;\n\nMetadata Parameters:\n- Target Primary Keyword: <mark>[PRIMARY_KEYWORD]</mark>\n- Secondary Keywords: <mark>[SECONDARY_KEYWORDS]</mark>\n- Target Audience: <mark>[TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Senior Go Engineers, Cloud DevOps Specialists]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Analyze the article content and keyword intent.\n2. Generate:\n   - 5 Title Tag Options (under 60 characters each):\n     - How-To / Problem-Solution title.\n     - Direct technical reference title.\n     - Actionable guide title.\n     - Comparison or best-practice title.\n     - Question-based search title.\n   - 3 Meta Description Options (140 to 155 characters each):\n     - Direct, engaging, incorporating the primary keyword naturally, ending with an active call to action.\n   - Primary H1 Heading: Optimized for on-page hierarchy and reader clarity.\n   - Recommended URL Slug: Clean, hyphen-separated, keyword-rich slug (e.g., /guides/kubernetes-multi-tenant-isolation).\n   - Open Graph (Social) Card Copy: Compelling title (under 70 chars) and description (under 120 chars) for LinkedIn and Twitter/X previews.\n3. Apply Microsoft Writing Style Guide: clear, active voice, sentence case, and no em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the metadata options, character count verifications, and social preview copy in Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are an SEO content specialist and technical copywriter. Generate high-ranking metadata and compelling title options for a technical article.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your draft technical guide or blog post (.md, .txt, or .docx).\n- Or paste the article text below:\n<article_content>\n[PASTE TECHNICAL ARTICLE OR DOC PAGE HERE]\n</article_content>\n\nMetadata Parameters:\n- Target Primary Keyword: [PRIMARY_KEYWORD]\n- Secondary Keywords: [SECONDARY_KEYWORDS]\n- Target Audience: [TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Senior Go Engineers, Cloud DevOps Specialists]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Analyze the article content and keyword intent.\n2. Generate:\n   - 5 Title Tag Options (under 60 characters each):\n     - How-To / Problem-Solution title.\n     - Direct technical reference title.\n     - Actionable guide title.\n     - Comparison or best-practice title.\n     - Question-based search title.\n   - 3 Meta Description Options (140 to 155 characters each):\n     - Direct, engaging, incorporating the primary keyword naturally, ending with an active call to action.\n   - Primary H1 Heading: Optimized for on-page hierarchy and reader clarity.\n   - Recommended URL Slug: Clean, hyphen-separated, keyword-rich slug (e.g., /guides/kubernetes-multi-tenant-isolation).\n   - Open Graph (Social) Card Copy: Compelling title (under 70 chars) and description (under 120 chars) for LinkedIn and Twitter/X previews.\n3. Apply Microsoft Writing Style Guide: clear, active voice, sentence case, and no em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the metadata options, character count verifications, and social preview copy in Markdown.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Specify your target search keyword to ensure title tags remain under 60 characters and meta descriptions stay within the 140 to 155 character sweet spot.",
