    "id": "p46",
    "number": "46",
    "categoryId": "drafting",
    "categoryName": "Drafting & Content Creation",
    "title": "Write a Release Summary",
    "useCase": "Create concise, high-impact release summaries for email announcements and in-app modals",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a product marketing technical writer. Write an engaging, high-impact release summary announcing <mark>[PRODUCT_OR_FEATURE]</mark> <mark>[VERSION_NUMBER]</mark>.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your technical changelog or sprint release notes (.md, .txt, or .docx).\n- Or provide release details below:\nProduct / Feature Name: <mark>[PRODUCT_OR_FEATURE]</mark>\nVersion / Release Name: <mark>[VERSION_NUMBER]</mark>\nRelease Date: <mark>[RELEASE_DATE]</mark>\nTarget Audience: <mark>[TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Workspace Administrators, Developers, Active Daily Users]</mark>\nCore Improvements (3 to 5 highlights):\n<mark>[LIST KEY HIGHLIGHTS HERE]</mark>\nCall to Action Link / Button: <mark>[CTA_LINK, e.g., Read Full Documentation / Upgrade Now / Open Dashboard]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Create three distinct communication formats tailored for distribution channels:\n   - Format 1: In-App Product Modal (under 150 words): Snappy title, 3 bullet points with bold keywords, and primary CTA button.\n   - Format 2: Customer Email Announcement (250 to 350 words): Catchy subject line, preview text, value-driven intro paragraph, feature breakdown, and next steps.\n   - Format 3: Slack / Microsoft Teams Channel Announcement: Formatted message with emojis, key takeaways, and documentation link.\n2. Emphasize user outcomes (time saved, productivity gained, enhanced security) rather than pure code changes.\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: energetic, active voice, sentence case, and zero em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput all three formatted summaries clearly labeled in Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a product marketing technical writer. Write an engaging, high-impact release summary announcing [PRODUCT_OR_FEATURE] [VERSION_NUMBER].\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your technical changelog or sprint release notes (.md, .txt, or .docx).\n- Or provide release details below:\nProduct / Feature Name: [PRODUCT_OR_FEATURE]\nVersion / Release Name: [VERSION_NUMBER]\nRelease Date: [RELEASE_DATE]\nTarget Audience: [TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Workspace Administrators, Developers, Active Daily Users]\nCore Improvements (3 to 5 highlights):\n[LIST KEY HIGHLIGHTS HERE]\nCall to Action Link / Button: [CTA_LINK, e.g., Read Full Documentation / Upgrade Now / Open Dashboard]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Create three distinct communication formats tailored for distribution channels:\n   - Format 1: In-App Product Modal (under 150 words): Snappy title, 3 bullet points with bold keywords, and primary CTA button.\n   - Format 2: Customer Email Announcement (250 to 350 words): Catchy subject line, preview text, value-driven intro paragraph, feature breakdown, and next steps.\n   - Format 3: Slack / Microsoft Teams Channel Announcement: Formatted message with emojis, key takeaways, and documentation link.\n2. Emphasize user outcomes (time saved, productivity gained, enhanced security) rather than pure code changes.\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: energetic, active voice, sentence case, and zero em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput all three formatted summaries clearly labeled in Markdown.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Attach your technical changelog to generate multi-channel announcements (in-app modal, email blast, Slack message) in one execution.",
