    "badgeColor": "#f59e0b",
    "promptText": "You are a Senior Technical Writer converting a raw spoken transcript into a polished, task-based documentation guide.\n\nTransform the following spoken transcript into clear, structured procedural documentation.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your video, meeting, or demo transcript file (.txt, .vtt, or .srt).\n- Or paste the raw transcript here:\n<mark>[PASTE RAW TRANSCRIPT HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;parameters&gt;\n- Document title: <mark>[DESIRED GUIDE TITLE]</mark>\n- Target audience: <mark>[TARGET AUDIENCE]</mark>\n- Core user goal: <mark>[WHAT THE READER WILL ACCOMPLISH]</mark>\n- Style guideline: Microsoft Writing Style Guide (active voice, numbered procedural steps, second person).\n&lt;/parameters&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Remove all spoken conversational filler, presenter banter, false starts, and off-topic tangents.\n2. Extract the actual logical workflow demonstrated by the speaker.\n3. Structure the output into:\n   - Overview: 2-sentence summary of the task.\n   - Prerequisites: Bulleted list of tools, permissions, and environment setup mentioned.\n   - Step-by-Step Instructions: Numbered procedural steps with UI elements in bold and code commands in backticks.\n   - Expected Result: What the user sees upon successful completion.\n   - Edge Cases or Gotchas: Practical tips mentioned casually by the speaker during the recording.\n4. Note any unclear steps where the speaker skipped an action on screen with a <mark>[VERIFY: ...]</mark> bracket.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nProvide a complete, standalone Markdown guide.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a Senior Technical Writer converting a raw spoken transcript into a polished, task-based documentation guide.\n\nTransform the following spoken transcript into clear, structured procedural documentation.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your video, meeting, or demo transcript file (.txt, .vtt, or .srt).\n- Or paste the raw transcript here:\n[PASTE RAW TRANSCRIPT HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<parameters>\n- Document title: [DESIRED GUIDE TITLE]\n- Target audience: [TARGET AUDIENCE]\n- Core user goal: [WHAT THE READER WILL ACCOMPLISH]\n- Style guideline: Microsoft Writing Style Guide (active voice, numbered procedural steps, second person).\n</parameters>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Remove all spoken conversational filler, presenter banter, false starts, and off-topic tangents.\n2. Extract the actual logical workflow demonstrated by the speaker.\n3. Structure the output into:\n   - Overview: 2-sentence summary of the task.\n   - Prerequisites: Bulleted list of tools, permissions, and environment setup mentioned.\n   - Step-by-Step Instructions: Numbered procedural steps with UI elements in bold and code commands in backticks.\n   - Expected Result: What the user sees upon successful completion.\n   - Edge Cases or Gotchas: Practical tips mentioned casually by the speaker during the recording.\n4. Note any unclear steps where the speaker skipped an action on screen with a [VERIFY: ...] bracket.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nProvide a complete, standalone Markdown guide.\n</output_format>",
