    "title": "Write a Video Script",
    "useCase": "Write a high-retention video script with dual-column audio and visual cues",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#f59e0b",
    "promptText": "You are a Technical Video Producer and instructional scriptwriter.\n\nWrite a compelling, high-retention technical video script for <mark>[VIDEO TOPIC OR FEATURE NAME]</mark>.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (optional):\n- Attach your feature PRD, written tutorial, or product release doc.\n- Or paste the technical background notes here:\n<mark>[PASTE TECHNICAL OVERVIEW OR TUTORIAL CONTENT HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;parameters&gt;\n- Video title: <mark>[DESIRED VIDEO TITLE]</mark>\n- Target video duration: <mark>[e.g., 2 minutes / 5 minutes / 10 minutes]</mark>\n- Target viewer: <mark>[e.g., Frontend Engineers, Product Managers, First-Time Users]</mark>\n- Tone: <mark>[e.g., Energetic, instructional, concise, developer-friendly]</mark>\n&lt;/parameters&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Structure the script into:\n   - The Hook (First 15 seconds): Address a real developer pain point immediately. No intro fluff.\n   - The Solution Overview: 30-second high-level demonstration of what we are building.\n   - Step-by-Step Walkthrough: The core demonstration divided into clear, numbered stages.\n   - Verification &amp; Testing: Show the working result on screen.\n   - Call to Action &amp; Wrap-up: Next steps, docs link, and subscribe prompt.\n2. Format the script as a Two-Column Table:\n   | Timestamp | Visual / Screen Action (What the viewer sees) | Audio / Voiceover Narration (Word-for-word spoken script) |\n3. Keep spoken sentences short, conversational, and synchronized with on-screen cursor movements and terminal commands.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the two-column script table followed by production notes (required assets, screen resolution, sample code repo).\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a Technical Video Producer and instructional scriptwriter.\n\nWrite a compelling, high-retention technical video script for [VIDEO TOPIC OR FEATURE NAME].\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (optional):\n- Attach your feature PRD, written tutorial, or product release doc.\n- Or paste the technical background notes here:\n[PASTE TECHNICAL OVERVIEW OR TUTORIAL CONTENT HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<parameters>\n- Video title: [DESIRED VIDEO TITLE]\n- Target video duration: [e.g., 2 minutes / 5 minutes / 10 minutes]\n- Target viewer: [e.g., Frontend Engineers, Product Managers, First-Time Users]\n- Tone: [e.g., Energetic, instructional, concise, developer-friendly]\n</parameters>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Structure the script into:\n   - The Hook (First 15 seconds): Address a real developer pain point immediately. No intro fluff.\n   - The Solution Overview: 30-second high-level demonstration of what we are building.\n   - Step-by-Step Walkthrough: The core demonstration divided into clear, numbered stages.\n   - Verification & Testing: Show the working result on screen.\n   - Call to Action & Wrap-up: Next steps, docs link, and subscribe prompt.\n2. Format the script as a Two-Column Table:\n   | Timestamp | Visual / Screen Action (What the viewer sees) | Audio / Voiceover Narration (Word-for-word spoken script) |\n3. Keep spoken sentences short, conversational, and synchronized with on-screen cursor movements and terminal commands.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the two-column script table followed by production notes (required assets, screen resolution, sample code repo).\n</output_format>",
