    "title": "Convert Prose to Structured Docs",
    "useCase": "Convert unstructured engineering narratives or meeting notes into structured documentation",
    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#f59e0b",
    "promptText": "You are a Lead Technical Writer transforming unstructured engineering brain-dumps into production-grade documentation.\n\nConvert the following unstructured narrative into clean, structured technical documentation.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your raw architecture notes, Slack thread export, meeting minutes, or design memo.\n- Or paste the raw text here:\n<mark>[PASTE UNSTRUCTURED NOTES OR SLACK CONVERSATION HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;parameters&gt;\n- Document type: <mark>[e.g., How-to Guide / Architecture Decision Record (ADR) / System Overview]</mark>\n- Target audience: <mark>[TARGET AUDIENCE]</mark>\n- Primary takeaway: <mark>[WHAT THE READER MUST UNDERSTAND OR EXECUTE]</mark>\n&lt;/parameters&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Extract all implicit decisions, architectural choices, and technical procedures from the text.\n2. Filter out conversational banter, tentative speculation, and outdated brainstorms.\n3. Organize into a structured document featuring:\n   - Context &amp; Motivation: Why this system or process exists.\n   - Architecture &amp; Core Components: Clear bulleted explanation of how pieces connect.\n   - Standard Operating Procedure: Numbered, sequential steps for execution.\n   - Configuration Reference: Table of parameters, environment variables, or settings.\n   - Known Gotchas &amp; Troubleshooting: Common edge cases discovered during development.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete structured document in Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a Lead Technical Writer transforming unstructured engineering brain-dumps into production-grade documentation.\n\nConvert the following unstructured narrative into clean, structured technical documentation.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your raw architecture notes, Slack thread export, meeting minutes, or design memo.\n- Or paste the raw text here:\n[PASTE UNSTRUCTURED NOTES OR SLACK CONVERSATION HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<parameters>\n- Document type: [e.g., How-to Guide / Architecture Decision Record (ADR) / System Overview]\n- Target audience: [TARGET AUDIENCE]\n- Primary takeaway: [WHAT THE READER MUST UNDERSTAND OR EXECUTE]\n</parameters>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Extract all implicit decisions, architectural choices, and technical procedures from the text.\n2. Filter out conversational banter, tentative speculation, and outdated brainstorms.\n3. Organize into a structured document featuring:\n   - Context & Motivation: Why this system or process exists.\n   - Architecture & Core Components: Clear bulleted explanation of how pieces connect.\n   - Standard Operating Procedure: Numbered, sequential steps for execution.\n   - Configuration Reference: Table of parameters, environment variables, or settings.\n   - Known Gotchas & Troubleshooting: Common edge cases discovered during development.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete structured document in Markdown.\n</output_format>",
