    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#f59e0b",
    "promptText": "You are a Content Repurposing Strategist and Technical Marketing Writer.\n\nRepurpose the following technical documentation article across multiple target communication channels.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach the original technical document (.md, .pdf, or .docx).\n- Or paste the technical article here:\n<mark>[PASTE SOURCE TECHNICAL ARTICLE HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;parameters&gt;\n- Core feature or topic: <mark>[TOPIC OR FEATURE NAME]</mark>\n- Target channels needed: <mark>[e.g., Developer Blog Post, Customer Newsletter Blurb, LinkedIn Post, Slack Announcement]</mark>\n&lt;/parameters&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\nAdapt the source material into 4 distinct formats:\n1. Developer Blog Post Outline: Catchy hook, technical architecture breakdown, code walkthrough, and conclusion.\n2. In-App Product Announcement Modal: Headline (max 8 words), 3-sentence value summary, and primary CTA.\n3. LinkedIn Thought Leadership Post: Curiosity-driven hook, key problem solved, bulleted technical insights, and discussion prompt.\n4. Internal Sales &amp; Support Enablement Cheat Sheet: 3-bullet elevator pitch, top 3 customer FAQs, and competitor differentiators.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nPresent each channel adaptation under its own clear section in Markdown with character counts and recommended visual assets.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a Content Repurposing Strategist and Technical Marketing Writer.\n\nRepurpose the following technical documentation article across multiple target communication channels.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach the original technical document (.md, .pdf, or .docx).\n- Or paste the technical article here:\n[PASTE SOURCE TECHNICAL ARTICLE HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<parameters>\n- Core feature or topic: [TOPIC OR FEATURE NAME]\n- Target channels needed: [e.g., Developer Blog Post, Customer Newsletter Blurb, LinkedIn Post, Slack Announcement]\n</parameters>\n\n<instructions>\nAdapt the source material into 4 distinct formats:\n1. Developer Blog Post Outline: Catchy hook, technical architecture breakdown, code walkthrough, and conclusion.\n2. In-App Product Announcement Modal: Headline (max 8 words), 3-sentence value summary, and primary CTA.\n3. LinkedIn Thought Leadership Post: Curiosity-driven hook, key problem solved, bulleted technical insights, and discussion prompt.\n4. Internal Sales & Support Enablement Cheat Sheet: 3-bullet elevator pitch, top 3 customer FAQs, and competitor differentiators.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nPresent each channel adaptation under its own clear section in Markdown with character counts and recommended visual assets.\n</output_format>",
