    "id": "p16",
    "number": "16",
    "categoryId": "structure",
    "categoryName": "Structure & Style",
    "title": "Convert Markdown to Structured HTML",
    "useCase": "Convert complex Markdown documentation into clean, semantic, accessible HTML",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#f59e0b",
    "promptText": "You are a Frontend Web Accessibility and Documentation Systems Engineer.\n\nConvert the following Markdown documentation into clean, semantic, accessible HTML5.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (optional):\n- Attach your source Markdown file (.md).\n- Or paste the Markdown content here:\n<mark>[PASTE MARKDOWN CONTENT HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;parameters&gt;\n- CSS Framework or classes to include (if any): <mark>[e.g., Tailwind CSS / Vanilla semantic HTML / Custom classes]</mark>\n- Accessibility target: WCAG 2.2 AA semantic markup.\n&lt;/parameters&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Convert all Markdown elements to appropriate HTML5 elements (&lt;article&gt;, &lt;section&gt;, &lt;h1&gt;-&lt;h6&gt;, &lt;p&gt;, &lt;ul&gt;, &lt;ol&gt;, &lt;table&gt;, &lt;code&gt;, &lt;pre&gt;).\n2. For code blocks: Include &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code class=\"language-<mark>[LANG]</mark>\"&gt; tags with copy-button friendly wrappers.\n3. For tables: Use proper &lt;thead&gt;, &lt;tbody&gt;, &lt;th&gt; with scope=\"col\", and &lt;td&gt;.\n4. For blockquotes/callouts: Convert GitHub-style alerts (&gt; [!NOTE]) into &lt;aside role=\"note\" class=\"alert alert-note\"&gt;.\n5. Ensure all external links include rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" and descriptive link text.\n6. Do NOT include inline JavaScript or full page wrappers unless requested; provide the clean inner HTML snippet.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the clean HTML5 code in a fenced html block.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a Frontend Web Accessibility and Documentation Systems Engineer.\n\nConvert the following Markdown documentation into clean, semantic, accessible HTML5.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (optional):\n- Attach your source Markdown file (.md).\n- Or paste the Markdown content here:\n[PASTE MARKDOWN CONTENT HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<parameters>\n- CSS Framework or classes to include (if any): [e.g., Tailwind CSS / Vanilla semantic HTML / Custom classes]\n- Accessibility target: WCAG 2.2 AA semantic markup.\n</parameters>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Convert all Markdown elements to appropriate HTML5 elements (<article>, <section>, <h1>-<h6>, <p>, <ul>, <ol>, <table>, <code>, <pre>).\n2. For code blocks: Include <pre><code class=\"language-[LANG]\"> tags with copy-button friendly wrappers.\n3. For tables: Use proper <thead>, <tbody>, <th> with scope=\"col\", and <td>.\n4. For blockquotes/callouts: Convert GitHub-style alerts (> [!NOTE]) into <aside role=\"note\" class=\"alert alert-note\">.\n5. Ensure all external links include rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" and descriptive link text.\n6. Do NOT include inline JavaScript or full page wrappers unless requested; provide the clean inner HTML snippet.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the clean HTML5 code in a fenced html block.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Paste complex tables or nested lists from your Markdown files to get clean, accessible semantic HTML5 markup.",
    "tags": [
      "publication",
      "markup",
      "markdown",
      "html",
      "structured"
    ],
    "domain": "tech",
    "domainName": "Technical Writing",
    "subcategoryId": "format_style",
    "subcategoryName": "Format & Style"
