    "id": "p48",
    "number": "48",
    "categoryId": "strategy",
    "categoryName": "Strategy & Planning",
    "title": "Prepare Docs for Static Site Publishing",
    "useCase": "Format raw Markdown with validated frontmatter, callouts, and components for docs engines",
    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#14b8a6",
    "promptText": "You are a Docs-as-Code publishing specialist. Convert raw Markdown content into a fully formatted, production-ready documentation page for <mark>[STATIC_SITE_GENERATOR]</mark>.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your raw draft article or markdown file (.md or .txt).\n- Or paste your raw content below:\nTarget Static Site Generator: <mark>[STATIC_SITE_GENERATOR, e.g., Docusaurus, MkDocs Material, Nextra, Starlight/Astro, Hugo]</mark>\nPage Title: <mark>[PAGE_TITLE]</mark>\nSidebar Position / Order: <mark>[SIDEBAR_POSITION]</mark>\nDescription: <mark>[META_DESCRIPTION]</mark>\nTags: <mark>[TAGS, e.g., api, authentication, v2]</mark>\n&lt;raw_content&gt;\n<mark>[PASTE RAW MARKDOWN OR DRAFT HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/raw_content&gt;\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Construct the appropriate YAML or TOML frontmatter required by the specified static site generator (title, description, sidebar_label, sidebar_position, tags).\n2. Transform inline formatting into engine-supported components:\n   - Convert plain notes or warnings into native admonitions/callouts (e.g., :::note / :::tip / :::warning in Docusaurus, or !!! note in MkDocs).\n   - Format multi-language code snippets into tabbed blocks where relevant (e.g., cURL, Node.js, Python).\n   - Ensure image paths follow asset conventions (e.g., ./assets/image.png) with valid alt text.\n   - Clean up heading hierarchy (single H1 derived from frontmatter or page title, followed by sequential H2 and H3 headings).\n3. Validate that no broken Markdown syntax, invalid HTML tags, or unclosed backticks exist.\n4. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: active voice, clear headings, and zero em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete, publication-ready Markdown file with frontmatter in a fenced markdown code block.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a Docs-as-Code publishing specialist. Convert raw Markdown content into a fully formatted, production-ready documentation page for [STATIC_SITE_GENERATOR].\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your raw draft article or markdown file (.md or .txt).\n- Or paste your raw content below:\nTarget Static Site Generator: [STATIC_SITE_GENERATOR, e.g., Docusaurus, MkDocs Material, Nextra, Starlight/Astro, Hugo]\nPage Title: [PAGE_TITLE]\nSidebar Position / Order: [SIDEBAR_POSITION]\nDescription: [META_DESCRIPTION]\nTags: [TAGS, e.g., api, authentication, v2]\n<raw_content>\n[PASTE RAW MARKDOWN OR DRAFT HERE]\n</raw_content>\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Construct the appropriate YAML or TOML frontmatter required by the specified static site generator (title, description, sidebar_label, sidebar_position, tags).\n2. Transform inline formatting into engine-supported components:\n   - Convert plain notes or warnings into native admonitions/callouts (e.g., :::note / :::tip / :::warning in Docusaurus, or !!! note in MkDocs).\n   - Format multi-language code snippets into tabbed blocks where relevant (e.g., cURL, Node.js, Python).\n   - Ensure image paths follow asset conventions (e.g., ./assets/image.png) with valid alt text.\n   - Clean up heading hierarchy (single H1 derived from frontmatter or page title, followed by sequential H2 and H3 headings).\n3. Validate that no broken Markdown syntax, invalid HTML tags, or unclosed backticks exist.\n4. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: active voice, clear headings, and zero em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete, publication-ready Markdown file with frontmatter in a fenced markdown code block.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Specify your static site generator (Docusaurus, MkDocs Material, Starlight) so callouts and tabs use native engine syntax.",
