    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a Lead Documentation Architect designing reusable documentation templates.\n\nCreate a production-ready documentation page template for a <mark>[DOCUMENTATION TYPE, e.g., How-to Guide / API Endpoint / Architecture Overview / Troubleshooting Playbook]</mark>.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (optional):\n- Attach your existing templates, design system requirements, or sample docs.\n- Or describe your documentation format requirements here:\n<mark>[DESCRIBE TARGET DOCUMENTATION TYPE AND FORMAT REQUIREMENTS HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;parameters&gt;\n- Documentation type: <mark>[DOCUMENTATION TYPE]</mark>\n- Static site generator / platform: <mark>[e.g., Docusaurus, MkDocs, Mintlify, Starlight, GitBook]</mark>\n- Target audience: <mark>[TARGET AUDIENCE]</mark>\n&lt;/parameters&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Create a complete, copy-pasteable Markdown template with:\n   - Frontmatter metadata block (title, description, tags, slug, last_updated).\n   - Document Title and Purpose Statement placeholder.\n   - Prerequisites &amp; Permissions section.\n   - Conceptual Diagram or Architecture placeholder.\n   - Step-by-Step Instructions with sample code fences, admonition callouts, and UI highlights.\n   - Verification / Next Steps section.\n   - Related Resources &amp; Troubleshooting links.\n2. Include inline HTML comments (&lt;!-- INSTRUCTIONS FOR WRITERS --&gt;) guiding contributors on what to write in each section and common pitfalls to avoid.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete Markdown template with frontmatter and inline contributor guidance comments.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a Lead Documentation Architect designing reusable documentation templates.\n\nCreate a production-ready documentation page template for a [DOCUMENTATION TYPE, e.g., How-to Guide / API Endpoint / Architecture Overview / Troubleshooting Playbook].\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (optional):\n- Attach your existing templates, design system requirements, or sample docs.\n- Or describe your documentation format requirements here:\n[DESCRIBE TARGET DOCUMENTATION TYPE AND FORMAT REQUIREMENTS HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<parameters>\n- Documentation type: [DOCUMENTATION TYPE]\n- Static site generator / platform: [e.g., Docusaurus, MkDocs, Mintlify, Starlight, GitBook]\n- Target audience: [TARGET AUDIENCE]\n</parameters>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Create a complete, copy-pasteable Markdown template with:\n   - Frontmatter metadata block (title, description, tags, slug, last_updated).\n   - Document Title and Purpose Statement placeholder.\n   - Prerequisites & Permissions section.\n   - Conceptual Diagram or Architecture placeholder.\n   - Step-by-Step Instructions with sample code fences, admonition callouts, and UI highlights.\n   - Verification / Next Steps section.\n   - Related Resources & Troubleshooting links.\n2. Include inline HTML comments (<!-- INSTRUCTIONS FOR WRITERS -->) guiding contributors on what to write in each section and common pitfalls to avoid.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete Markdown template with frontmatter and inline contributor guidance comments.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Specify your static site generator (e.g., Docusaurus or Mintlify) so the template includes the correct frontmatter and callout syntax.",
