    "promptText": "You are a principal documentation strategist and information architect. Conduct a comprehensive content audit and gap analysis on an existing documentation library.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your sitemap, documentation export, table of contents, or doc inventory spreadsheet (.csv, .xlsx, .md, or .json).\n- Or paste your list of existing documentation pages here:\n<mark>[PASTE EXISTING DOC INVENTORY HERE]</mark>\n\nProduct context:\n- Product Overview: <mark>[PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION]</mark>\n- Target Audience: <mark>[TARGET_AUDIENCE]</mark>\n- Recent Product Changes or Uncovered Customer Friction: <mark>[RECENT_CHANGES_OR_PAIN_POINTS]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Evaluate the existing content against the product capabilities and audience needs.\n2. Group your analysis into four key assessment categories:\n   - Missing Content (Gaps): Essential user journeys, prerequisites, edge cases, and onboarding steps with zero documentation.\n   - Outdated or Inaccurate Content: Deprecated features, superseded UI instructions, outdated code snippets, or invalid endpoints.\n   - Redundant or Overlapping Content: Duplicate articles, conflicting instructions across pages, and fragmented topics.\n   - Structural &amp; Quality Issues: Information architecture weaknesses, broken progressive disclosure, and missing search keywords.\n3. Present your findings in a prioritized Action Matrix:\n   - Table columns: Priority (P0/P1/P2) | Article / Area | Issue Category | Detailed Finding | Recommended Action | Effort (Low/Med/High).\n4. Provide a 3-phase remediation roadmap to implement the fixes efficiently.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete audit findings, prioritized Action Matrix, and roadmap in Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a principal documentation strategist and information architect. Conduct a comprehensive content audit and gap analysis on an existing documentation library.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your sitemap, documentation export, table of contents, or doc inventory spreadsheet (.csv, .xlsx, .md, or .json).\n- Or paste your list of existing documentation pages here:\n[PASTE EXISTING DOC INVENTORY HERE]\n\nProduct context:\n- Product Overview: [PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION]\n- Target Audience: [TARGET_AUDIENCE]\n- Recent Product Changes or Uncovered Customer Friction: [RECENT_CHANGES_OR_PAIN_POINTS]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Evaluate the existing content against the product capabilities and audience needs.\n2. Group your analysis into four key assessment categories:\n   - Missing Content (Gaps): Essential user journeys, prerequisites, edge cases, and onboarding steps with zero documentation.\n   - Outdated or Inaccurate Content: Deprecated features, superseded UI instructions, outdated code snippets, or invalid endpoints.\n   - Redundant or Overlapping Content: Duplicate articles, conflicting instructions across pages, and fragmented topics.\n   - Structural & Quality Issues: Information architecture weaknesses, broken progressive disclosure, and missing search keywords.\n3. Present your findings in a prioritized Action Matrix:\n   - Table columns: Priority (P0/P1/P2) | Article / Area | Issue Category | Detailed Finding | Recommended Action | Effort (Low/Med/High).\n4. Provide a 3-phase remediation roadmap to implement the fixes efficiently.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete audit findings, prioritized Action Matrix, and roadmap in Markdown.\n</output_format>",
