    "title": "Write a Docs-as-Code Proposal",
    "useCase": "Present a business case to engineering leadership for Git-based docs workflows",
    "level": "Advanced",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a staff technical writer and developer experience advocate. Write an internal executive proposal and business case advocating for a modern Docs-as-Code workflow.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nContext and current environment:\n- Company Profile: <mark>[COMPANY_TYPE, e.g., SaaS startup, Enterprise Fintech]</mark>\n- Current Documentation Tool: <mark>[CURRENT_TOOL, e.g., Confluence, Google Docs, Zendesk, CMS]</mark>\n- Proposed Docs-as-Code Stack: <mark>[PROPOSED_STACK, e.g., Markdown/MDX, GitHub, Docusaurus/MkDocs, Vercel/GitHub Actions]</mark>\n- Main Pain Points Today: <mark>[PAIN_POINTS, e.g., Docs out of sync with code, no PR review, writer bottleneck, poor versioning]</mark>\n- Target Decision Makers: <mark>[DECISION_MAKERS, e.g., VP of Engineering, Head of Product, Lead Architect]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Structure the proposal into an executive-ready business proposal:\n   - Executive Summary: The problem, the proposed solution, and high-level return on investment (ROI).\n   - Problem Statement: Quantify developer friction, outdated docs risk, customer support ticket load, and slow release cycles.\n   - The Docs-as-Code Solution: Explain core principles (version control alongside code, PR-based technical reviews, automated CI/CD linting, and preview deploys).\n   - Comparison Matrix: Current Tool vs. Docs-as-Code across Collaboration, Versioning, Review Velocity, Search, and Maintenance Costs.\n   - Implementation Plan: A realistic 4-phase rollout (PoC, Tooling setup, Content Migration, Training).\n   - Risk Analysis &amp; Mitigations: Address non-technical contributors, WYSIWYG editing, and change management.\n   - Recommended Next Steps: Concrete actions to launch a 30-day proof of concept.\n2. Adhere to the Microsoft Writing Style Guide: confident, data-driven, active voice, and professional tone.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete proposal in professional Markdown format.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a staff technical writer and developer experience advocate. Write an internal executive proposal and business case advocating for a modern Docs-as-Code workflow.\n\n<input_sources>\nContext and current environment:\n- Company Profile: [COMPANY_TYPE, e.g., SaaS startup, Enterprise Fintech]\n- Current Documentation Tool: [CURRENT_TOOL, e.g., Confluence, Google Docs, Zendesk, CMS]\n- Proposed Docs-as-Code Stack: [PROPOSED_STACK, e.g., Markdown/MDX, GitHub, Docusaurus/MkDocs, Vercel/GitHub Actions]\n- Main Pain Points Today: [PAIN_POINTS, e.g., Docs out of sync with code, no PR review, writer bottleneck, poor versioning]\n- Target Decision Makers: [DECISION_MAKERS, e.g., VP of Engineering, Head of Product, Lead Architect]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Structure the proposal into an executive-ready business proposal:\n   - Executive Summary: The problem, the proposed solution, and high-level return on investment (ROI).\n   - Problem Statement: Quantify developer friction, outdated docs risk, customer support ticket load, and slow release cycles.\n   - The Docs-as-Code Solution: Explain core principles (version control alongside code, PR-based technical reviews, automated CI/CD linting, and preview deploys).\n   - Comparison Matrix: Current Tool vs. Docs-as-Code across Collaboration, Versioning, Review Velocity, Search, and Maintenance Costs.\n   - Implementation Plan: A realistic 4-phase rollout (PoC, Tooling setup, Content Migration, Training).\n   - Risk Analysis & Mitigations: Address non-technical contributors, WYSIWYG editing, and change management.\n   - Recommended Next Steps: Concrete actions to launch a 30-day proof of concept.\n2. Adhere to the Microsoft Writing Style Guide: confident, data-driven, active voice, and professional tone.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete proposal in professional Markdown format.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Highlight engineering pull request velocity and reduced support ticket deflection metrics to persuade technical and finance leaders.",
