    "level": "Advanced",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a documentation program manager and lead technical writer. Create a comprehensive Stakeholder Communication Plan for a major documentation initiative.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your project charter, product timeline, or engineering sprint schedule (.docx, .pdf, or .md).\n- Or provide initiative details below:\nInitiative Name: <mark>[INITIATIVE_NAME, e.g., V2 API Redesign Documentation Overhaul]</mark>\nProduct / Engineering Release Date: <mark>[RELEASE_DATE]</mark>\nKey Stakeholder Groups: <mark>[STAKEHOLDERS, e.g., Engineering Leads, Product Managers, Developer Relations, Customer Support, Marketing]</mark>\nPrimary Communication Channels: <mark>[CHANNELS, e.g., Slack, Email, Bi-weekly sync, GitHub project board]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Structure the stakeholder communication plan:\n   - Executive Summary: Objective of the documentation overhaul and key milestones.\n   - Stakeholder Matrix (RACI):\n     - Table listing Stakeholder Group | Role | RACI Status (Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Informed) | Engagement Channel | Cadence.\n   - Review and Approval Workflows:\n     - Technical Accuracy Review: SLA (e.g., 3 business days), tools (GitHub PRs), and required engineer sign-offs.\n     - Product &amp; Legal Review: Compliance checks, brand alignment, and release gate sign-off.\n   - Communication Cadence: Format and schedule for weekly async progress broadcasts, blocker escalations, and sprint demos.\n   - Pre-Launch and Post-Launch Communication: Announcement templates for internal teams (Support, Sales Engineering) before external release.\n2. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: professional, concise, active voice, and zero em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete Stakeholder Communication Plan in Markdown format.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a documentation program manager and lead technical writer. Create a comprehensive Stakeholder Communication Plan for a major documentation initiative.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your project charter, product timeline, or engineering sprint schedule (.docx, .pdf, or .md).\n- Or provide initiative details below:\nInitiative Name: [INITIATIVE_NAME, e.g., V2 API Redesign Documentation Overhaul]\nProduct / Engineering Release Date: [RELEASE_DATE]\nKey Stakeholder Groups: [STAKEHOLDERS, e.g., Engineering Leads, Product Managers, Developer Relations, Customer Support, Marketing]\nPrimary Communication Channels: [CHANNELS, e.g., Slack, Email, Bi-weekly sync, GitHub project board]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Structure the stakeholder communication plan:\n   - Executive Summary: Objective of the documentation overhaul and key milestones.\n   - Stakeholder Matrix (RACI):\n     - Table listing Stakeholder Group | Role | RACI Status (Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Informed) | Engagement Channel | Cadence.\n   - Review and Approval Workflows:\n     - Technical Accuracy Review: SLA (e.g., 3 business days), tools (GitHub PRs), and required engineer sign-offs.\n     - Product & Legal Review: Compliance checks, brand alignment, and release gate sign-off.\n   - Communication Cadence: Format and schedule for weekly async progress broadcasts, blocker escalations, and sprint demos.\n   - Pre-Launch and Post-Launch Communication: Announcement templates for internal teams (Support, Sales Engineering) before external release.\n2. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: professional, concise, active voice, and zero em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete Stakeholder Communication Plan in Markdown format.\n</output_format>",
