    "categoryName": "Sample Product Documentation Prompts",
    "title": "Getting Started Guide",
    "useCase": "Scaffold an introductory guide that walks new users through initial onboarding",
    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a senior technical writer specializing in developer onboarding. Write an exceptional, frictionless Getting Started guide for <mark>[PRODUCT_NAME]</mark>.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your API spec (OpenAPI/Swagger JSON or YAML), CLI help dump, or onboarding design document.\n- Or provide product details below:\nProduct Name: <mark>[PRODUCT_NAME]</mark>\nProduct Purpose: <mark>[ONE_SENTENCE_VALUE_PROPOSITION]</mark>\nTarget Audience: <mark>[TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Frontend Engineers, Data Analysts, Node.js Developers]</mark>\nPrerequisites: [PREREQUISITES, e.g., Node.js v18+, API Key, Docker]\nCore First Task: <mark>[CORE_ACTION, e.g., Initializing the SDK, making your first authenticated request, deploying a starter template]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Review the input materials and construct a step-by-step onboarding guide.\n2. Structure the guide following progressive disclosure:\n   - What You Will Build / Learn: State the goal clearly in one introductory sentence.\n   - Prerequisites: Checkbox list with minimum versions and setup requirements.\n   - Step 1: Install and Configure: Show package manager install commands and environment variable setup.\n   - Step 2: Authenticate: Show how to pass credentials securely.\n   - Step 3: Run Your First Operation: Provide an executable, minimal code snippet with realistic dummy values.\n   - Step 4: Verify the Output: Show the expected response payload or CLI output.\n   - Next Steps: Bulleted links to conceptual architecture, API reference, and advanced tutorials.\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: use imperative verbs for step titles, second person ('you'), and callout blocks for important tips.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete Getting Started guide in clean Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a senior technical writer specializing in developer onboarding. Write an exceptional, frictionless Getting Started guide for [PRODUCT_NAME].\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your API spec (OpenAPI/Swagger JSON or YAML), CLI help dump, or onboarding design document.\n- Or provide product details below:\nProduct Name: [PRODUCT_NAME]\nProduct Purpose: [ONE_SENTENCE_VALUE_PROPOSITION]\nTarget Audience: [TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Frontend Engineers, Data Analysts, Node.js Developers]\nPrerequisites: [PREREQUISITES, e.g., Node.js v18+, API Key, Docker]\nCore First Task: [CORE_ACTION, e.g., Initializing the SDK, making your first authenticated request, deploying a starter template]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Review the input materials and construct a step-by-step onboarding guide.\n2. Structure the guide following progressive disclosure:\n   - What You Will Build / Learn: State the goal clearly in one introductory sentence.\n   - Prerequisites: Checkbox list with minimum versions and setup requirements.\n   - Step 1: Install and Configure: Show package manager install commands and environment variable setup.\n   - Step 2: Authenticate: Show how to pass credentials securely.\n   - Step 3: Run Your First Operation: Provide an executable, minimal code snippet with realistic dummy values.\n   - Step 4: Verify the Output: Show the expected response payload or CLI output.\n   - Next Steps: Bulleted links to conceptual architecture, API reference, and advanced tutorials.\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: use imperative verbs for step titles, second person ('you'), and callout blocks for important tips.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete Getting Started guide in clean Markdown.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Attach your OpenAPI schema or quickstart code sample so the AI extracts exact parameter names and executable code without hallucination.",
