    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are an API technical writer. Write a comprehensive, production-grade API reference page for a GET endpoint.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your OpenAPI/Swagger specification excerpt or JSON response payload.\n- Or specify endpoint parameters below:\nHTTP Method: GET\nEndpoint Path: [ENDPOINT_PATH, e.g., /v1/organizations/{org_id}/members]\nBase URL: <mark>[BASE_URL, e.g., https://api.example.com]</mark>\nSummary: <mark>[ONE_SENTENCE_PURPOSE]</mark>\nAuthentication Required: <mark>[AUTH_TYPE, e.g., Bearer token in Authorization header]</mark>\nPath Parameters: <mark>[PATH_PARAMETERS, e.g., org_id (string, required): unique organization identifier]</mark>\nQuery Parameters: <mark>[QUERY_PARAMETERS, e.g., limit (integer, optional, default 20), starting_after (string, optional)]</mark>\nSample Response JSON:\n<mark>[PASTE SAMPLE RESPONSE JSON HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Construct the API reference page in standard developer portal layout:\n   - Endpoint Title &amp; Method Badge: Clear HTTP verb and full path.\n   - Description: Explain what resource is fetched and common use cases.\n   - Authentication: Exact header structure and scopes required.\n   - Request Parameters: Table with Parameter Name | Type | Required/Optional | Default | Description.\n   - Request Example: Complete, copy-pasteable curl command including auth headers and sample query parameters.\n   - Response Payloads:\n     - 200 OK: Full annotated JSON schema and complete sample response.\n     - Error Status Codes: 400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized, 403 Forbidden, 404 Not Found, 429 Rate Limited.\n   - Edge Cases &amp; Rate Limits: Note pagination behavior, caching headers, and rate limit ceilings.\n2. Format table columns cleanly and ensure all JSON snippets are syntactically valid.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the reference documentation in GitHub-flavored Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are an API technical writer. Write a comprehensive, production-grade API reference page for a GET endpoint.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your OpenAPI/Swagger specification excerpt or JSON response payload.\n- Or specify endpoint parameters below:\nHTTP Method: GET\nEndpoint Path: [ENDPOINT_PATH, e.g., /v1/organizations/{org_id}/members]\nBase URL: [BASE_URL, e.g., https://api.example.com]\nSummary: [ONE_SENTENCE_PURPOSE]\nAuthentication Required: [AUTH_TYPE, e.g., Bearer token in Authorization header]\nPath Parameters: [PATH_PARAMETERS, e.g., org_id (string, required): unique organization identifier]\nQuery Parameters: [QUERY_PARAMETERS, e.g., limit (integer, optional, default 20), starting_after (string, optional)]\nSample Response JSON:\n[PASTE SAMPLE RESPONSE JSON HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Construct the API reference page in standard developer portal layout:\n   - Endpoint Title & Method Badge: Clear HTTP verb and full path.\n   - Description: Explain what resource is fetched and common use cases.\n   - Authentication: Exact header structure and scopes required.\n   - Request Parameters: Table with Parameter Name | Type | Required/Optional | Default | Description.\n   - Request Example: Complete, copy-pasteable curl command including auth headers and sample query parameters.\n   - Response Payloads:\n     - 200 OK: Full annotated JSON schema and complete sample response.\n     - Error Status Codes: 400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized, 403 Forbidden, 404 Not Found, 429 Rate Limited.\n   - Edge Cases & Rate Limits: Note pagination behavior, caching headers, and rate limit ceilings.\n2. Format table columns cleanly and ensure all JSON snippets are syntactically valid.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the reference documentation in GitHub-flavored Markdown.\n</output_format>",
