    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a specialist API technical writer. Create a complete, developer-friendly API reference page for a POST endpoint.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your OpenAPI/Swagger spec (.yaml or .json) or sample request and response payloads.\n- Or provide endpoint parameters below:\nHTTP Method: POST\nEndpoint Path: <mark>[ENDPOINT_PATH, e.g., /v1/webhooks/subscriptions]</mark>\nBase URL: <mark>[BASE_URL, e.g., https://api.example.com]</mark>\nPurpose: <mark>[ONE_SENTENCE_DESCRIPTION]</mark>\nAuthentication: <mark>[AUTH_METHOD, e.g., Bearer Token]</mark>\nHeaders: <mark>[REQUIRED_HEADERS, e.g., Content-Type: application/json, Idempotency-Key]</mark>\nSample Request Body (JSON):\n<mark>[PASTE SAMPLE REQUEST BODY HERE]</mark>\nSample Success Response (JSON):\n<mark>[PASTE SAMPLE SUCCESS RESPONSE HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Write the reference documentation covering:\n   - Header &amp; Endpoint Definition: Method, full URL path, and authentication prerequisites.\n   - Request Headers: Table listing required and optional HTTP headers.\n   - Request Body Attributes: Detailed table containing Field Name | Type | Required/Optional | Constraints/Validation | Description. Include nested object explanations.\n   - Code Example: Runnable curl request with complete JSON payload and sample headers.\n   - Success Response (201 Created / 200 OK): Response headers, status code, and full JSON body.\n   - Error Handling: Specific 4xx and 5xx responses (e.g., 400 Malformed JSON, 409 Conflict, 422 Unprocessable Entity) with concrete error payloads.\n   - Idempotency &amp; Retries: Guidance on safe retries using idempotency headers if supported.\n2. Follow the Microsoft Writing Style Guide: clear, active voice, sentence case, and no em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete API reference documentation in clean Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a specialist API technical writer. Create a complete, developer-friendly API reference page for a POST endpoint.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your OpenAPI/Swagger spec (.yaml or .json) or sample request and response payloads.\n- Or provide endpoint parameters below:\nHTTP Method: POST\nEndpoint Path: [ENDPOINT_PATH, e.g., /v1/webhooks/subscriptions]\nBase URL: [BASE_URL, e.g., https://api.example.com]\nPurpose: [ONE_SENTENCE_DESCRIPTION]\nAuthentication: [AUTH_METHOD, e.g., Bearer Token]\nHeaders: [REQUIRED_HEADERS, e.g., Content-Type: application/json, Idempotency-Key]\nSample Request Body (JSON):\n[PASTE SAMPLE REQUEST BODY HERE]\nSample Success Response (JSON):\n[PASTE SAMPLE SUCCESS RESPONSE HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Write the reference documentation covering:\n   - Header & Endpoint Definition: Method, full URL path, and authentication prerequisites.\n   - Request Headers: Table listing required and optional HTTP headers.\n   - Request Body Attributes: Detailed table containing Field Name | Type | Required/Optional | Constraints/Validation | Description. Include nested object explanations.\n   - Code Example: Runnable curl request with complete JSON payload and sample headers.\n   - Success Response (201 Created / 200 OK): Response headers, status code, and full JSON body.\n   - Error Handling: Specific 4xx and 5xx responses (e.g., 400 Malformed JSON, 409 Conflict, 422 Unprocessable Entity) with concrete error payloads.\n   - Idempotency & Retries: Guidance on safe retries using idempotency headers if supported.\n2. Follow the Microsoft Writing Style Guide: clear, active voice, sentence case, and no em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete API reference documentation in clean Markdown.\n</output_format>",
