    "categoryName": "Sample Product Documentation Prompts",
    "title": "Error Code Reference",
    "useCase": "Catalog system error codes with root causes, retry policies, and resolution steps",
    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a senior technical writer specializing in developer troubleshooting and error architectures. Create an exhaustive Error Code Reference page for <mark>[PRODUCT_NAME]</mark>.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your codebase error enum file, OpenAPI response components, or server logs (.json, .ts, .py, or .yaml).\n- Or provide error code context below:\nProduct Name: <mark>[PRODUCT_NAME]</mark>\nBase API URL: <mark>[BASE_URL]</mark>\nTarget Audience: <mark>[TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Integrating Developers, System Administrators]</mark>\nError Codes or Raw Error Responses:\n<mark>[PASTE ERROR CODES, SCHEMAS, OR SAMPLE RESPONSES HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Synthesize the error inputs into a standardized, developer-centric reference guide.\n2. Document the global error envelope format (standard JSON error structure with code, message, requestId, details, doc_url).\n3. For each error code, create a dedicated entry with:\n   - Error Code Identifier &amp; HTTP Status Code (e.g., `AUTH_INVALID_TOKEN` / 401).\n   - Human-Readable Meaning: Plain language explanation of what went wrong.\n   - Likely Root Causes: Bulleted list of the top technical reasons this error fires.\n   - Resolution Steps: Step-by-step instructions telling the developer exactly how to resolve the condition.\n   - Retry Policy: Explicit guidance (e.g., Safe to retry immediately, Retry with exponential backoff, Do not retry without code change).\n   - Sample Error Payload: Valid JSON snippet illustrating the exact server output.\n4. Conclude with a Quick Lookup Table: Error Code | HTTP Status | Short Description | Retryable (Yes/No).\n5. Apply Microsoft Writing Style Guide: direct, second person ('you'), clear headings, and zero em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete error reference in GitHub-flavored Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a senior technical writer specializing in developer troubleshooting and error architectures. Create an exhaustive Error Code Reference page for [PRODUCT_NAME].\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your codebase error enum file, OpenAPI response components, or server logs (.json, .ts, .py, or .yaml).\n- Or provide error code context below:\nProduct Name: [PRODUCT_NAME]\nBase API URL: [BASE_URL]\nTarget Audience: [TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Integrating Developers, System Administrators]\nError Codes or Raw Error Responses:\n[PASTE ERROR CODES, SCHEMAS, OR SAMPLE RESPONSES HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Synthesize the error inputs into a standardized, developer-centric reference guide.\n2. Document the global error envelope format (standard JSON error structure with code, message, requestId, details, doc_url).\n3. For each error code, create a dedicated entry with:\n   - Error Code Identifier & HTTP Status Code (e.g., `AUTH_INVALID_TOKEN` / 401).\n   - Human-Readable Meaning: Plain language explanation of what went wrong.\n   - Likely Root Causes: Bulleted list of the top technical reasons this error fires.\n   - Resolution Steps: Step-by-step instructions telling the developer exactly how to resolve the condition.\n   - Retry Policy: Explicit guidance (e.g., Safe to retry immediately, Retry with exponential backoff, Do not retry without code change).\n   - Sample Error Payload: Valid JSON snippet illustrating the exact server output.\n4. Conclude with a Quick Lookup Table: Error Code | HTTP Status | Short Description | Retryable (Yes/No).\n5. Apply Microsoft Writing Style Guide: direct, second person ('you'), clear headings, and zero em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete error reference in GitHub-flavored Markdown.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Attach your backend error enum or OpenAPI errors schema to ensure every status code has an actionable, step-by-step troubleshooting fix.",
