    "categoryName": "Sample Product Documentation Prompts",
    "title": "Conceptual Overview",
    "useCase": "Explain core concepts and architectural models before diving into step-by-step procedures",
    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a principal technical writer and systems educator. Write a lucid, illuminating Conceptual Overview for <mark>[PRODUCT_OR_FEATURE_NAME]</mark>.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your system architecture diagram, RFC, engineering design doc, or whiteboard transcript (.pdf, .md, or .docx).\n- Or provide background details below:\nProduct / Feature Name: <mark>[PRODUCT_OR_FEATURE_NAME]</mark>\nOne-Sentence Purpose: <mark>[ONE_SENTENCE_PURPOSE]</mark>\nTarget Audience: <mark>[TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Senior Architects, Junior Developers, IT Directors]</mark>\nCore Concepts to Explain: <mark>[LIST 2 TO 4 KEY CONCEPTS, e.g., Event Loop, Multi-Tenant Isolation, Distributed Consensus]</mark>\nReal-World Analogy (optional): <mark>[ANALOGY, e.g., like a postal sorting facility, like a bank ledger]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Structure the conceptual overview to provide deep mental models before users read tactical procedures:\n   - High-Level Summary: Explain the foundational value proposition and problem domain.\n   - The Mental Model: Use a lucid analogy or visual description to make abstract concepts tangible.\n   - Architecture &amp; Data Flow: Step-by-step narrative describing how data or control flows through the components.\n   - Mermaid Architecture Diagram: Generate a clean, error-free Mermaid flowchart showing the relationship between components.\n   - Key Entities &amp; Terminology: Define the primary nouns and objects in the system.\n   - Why This Matters: Explain how this architectural model benefits scalability, security, or developer productivity.\n   - What Next: Links directing users to the Quickstart and API Reference guides.\n2. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: active voice, clear headings, and zero em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the conceptual overview in Markdown, including a valid Mermaid code block.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a principal technical writer and systems educator. Write a lucid, illuminating Conceptual Overview for [PRODUCT_OR_FEATURE_NAME].\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your system architecture diagram, RFC, engineering design doc, or whiteboard transcript (.pdf, .md, or .docx).\n- Or provide background details below:\nProduct / Feature Name: [PRODUCT_OR_FEATURE_NAME]\nOne-Sentence Purpose: [ONE_SENTENCE_PURPOSE]\nTarget Audience: [TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., Senior Architects, Junior Developers, IT Directors]\nCore Concepts to Explain: [LIST 2 TO 4 KEY CONCEPTS, e.g., Event Loop, Multi-Tenant Isolation, Distributed Consensus]\nReal-World Analogy (optional): [ANALOGY, e.g., like a postal sorting facility, like a bank ledger]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Structure the conceptual overview to provide deep mental models before users read tactical procedures:\n   - High-Level Summary: Explain the foundational value proposition and problem domain.\n   - The Mental Model: Use a lucid analogy or visual description to make abstract concepts tangible.\n   - Architecture & Data Flow: Step-by-step narrative describing how data or control flows through the components.\n   - Mermaid Architecture Diagram: Generate a clean, error-free Mermaid flowchart showing the relationship between components.\n   - Key Entities & Terminology: Define the primary nouns and objects in the system.\n   - Why This Matters: Explain how this architectural model benefits scalability, security, or developer productivity.\n   - What Next: Links directing users to the Quickstart and API Reference guides.\n2. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: active voice, clear headings, and zero em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the conceptual overview in Markdown, including a valid Mermaid code block.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Attach your engineering architecture document (RFC/EDD). The prompt will generate a conceptual explanation along with a Mermaid diagram.",
