    "id": "p32",
    "number": "32",
    "categoryId": "apidocs",
    "categoryName": "Sample Product Documentation Prompts",
    "title": "Quickstart Guide",
    "useCase": "Get developers from zero to their first successful API call in under five minutes",
    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a developer experience (DevEx) technical writer. Write an ultra-fast, 5-minute Quickstart Guide for <mark>[PRODUCT_NAME]</mark>.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your API spec or working sample code snippet (.json, .yaml, .js, .py, or .sh).\n- Or provide quickstart details below:\nProduct Name: <mark>[PRODUCT_NAME]</mark>\nQuickstart Objective: <mark>[DESIRED_OUTCOME, e.g., Send your first SMS notification, Query a vector database, Generate an invoice]</mark>\nTarget Developer Language: <mark>[LANGUAGE, e.g., cURL, Node.js, Python, Go]</mark>\nBase URL / Test Environment: <mark>[BASE_URL]</mark>\nPrerequisites: [PREREQUISITES, e.g., Free API key, Node 18+]\nSample Payload or Command:\n<mark>[PASTE WORKING SAMPLE CODE OR PAYLOAD HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Optimize for Time-To-First-Hello-World (under 5 minutes):\n   - Goal Statement: Tell the developer in 1 sentence what they will accomplish.\n   - Step 1: Get Credentials: 2 sentences on grabbing an API key from the developer console.\n   - Step 2: Set Environment Variable: Show export command (e.g., export API_KEY=\"...\").\n   - Step 3: Run the Code: Provide a complete, single-file copy-pasteable script or curl command with realistic dummy data.\n   - Step 4: Verify Success: Show the exact JSON response they should receive.\n   - Troubleshooting: 3 quick bullet points on the most common first-run errors (e.g., 401 missing key, 400 invalid parameter).\n   - What to Explore Next: 3 bullet points with next steps.\n2. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: imperative verbs, second person ('you'), and no em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the quickstart guide in clean GitHub-flavored Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a developer experience (DevEx) technical writer. Write an ultra-fast, 5-minute Quickstart Guide for [PRODUCT_NAME].\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your API spec or working sample code snippet (.json, .yaml, .js, .py, or .sh).\n- Or provide quickstart details below:\nProduct Name: [PRODUCT_NAME]\nQuickstart Objective: [DESIRED_OUTCOME, e.g., Send your first SMS notification, Query a vector database, Generate an invoice]\nTarget Developer Language: [LANGUAGE, e.g., cURL, Node.js, Python, Go]\nBase URL / Test Environment: [BASE_URL]\nPrerequisites: [PREREQUISITES, e.g., Free API key, Node 18+]\nSample Payload or Command:\n[PASTE WORKING SAMPLE CODE OR PAYLOAD HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Optimize for Time-To-First-Hello-World (under 5 minutes):\n   - Goal Statement: Tell the developer in 1 sentence what they will accomplish.\n   - Step 1: Get Credentials: 2 sentences on grabbing an API key from the developer console.\n   - Step 2: Set Environment Variable: Show export command (e.g., export API_KEY=\"...\").\n   - Step 3: Run the Code: Provide a complete, single-file copy-pasteable script or curl command with realistic dummy data.\n   - Step 4: Verify Success: Show the exact JSON response they should receive.\n   - Troubleshooting: 3 quick bullet points on the most common first-run errors (e.g., 401 missing key, 400 invalid parameter).\n   - What to Explore Next: 3 bullet points with next steps.\n2. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: imperative verbs, second person ('you'), and no em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the quickstart guide in clean GitHub-flavored Markdown.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Ensure the code snippet is 100% self-contained and runnable without requiring multiple file configurations.",
    "tags": [
      "quickstart",
      "guide"
    ],
    "domain": "tech",
    "domainName": "Technical Writing",
    "subcategoryId": "draft_content",
    "subcategoryName": "Draft & Content"
