    "title": "PUT Endpoint Reference Page",
    "useCase": "Document update and replacement operations with request bodies and idempotency notes",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are an API technical writer. Write a comprehensive reference page for a REST API PUT endpoint.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your OpenAPI/Swagger definition or JSON payload schema (.json or .yaml).\n- Or provide endpoint parameters below:\nHTTP Method: PUT\nEndpoint Path: [ENDPOINT_PATH, e.g., /v1/customers/{customer_id}]\nBase URL: <mark>[BASE_URL, e.g., https://api.example.com]</mark>\nSummary / Purpose: <mark>[ONE_SENTENCE_PURPOSE]</mark>\nAuthentication: <mark>[AUTH_SCHEME, e.g., Bearer Token]</mark>\nPath Parameters: <mark>[PATH_PARAMETERS, e.g., customer_id (string, required): unique identifier of the customer]</mark>\nRequest Body (Full Replacement / Upsert):\n<mark>[PASTE SAMPLE REQUEST BODY HERE]</mark>\nSuccess Response (200 OK or 201 Created):\n<mark>[PASTE SAMPLE SUCCESS RESPONSE HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Document the PUT endpoint following RESTful standards:\n   - Clarify Semantics: Explicitly state whether this endpoint performs full resource replacement or upsert (create-or-replace) logic. Differentiate from PATCH.\n   - Path Parameters: Table with Parameter | Type | Required | Description.\n   - Request Headers: Specify Content-Type and optional headers like If-Match or Idempotency-Key.\n   - Request Body Schema: Comprehensive table detailing every property, type, required status, and constraints.\n   - Code Example: Runnable curl snippet demonstrating the PUT request with full payload.\n   - Response Schemas: Document 200 OK / 201 Created responses with complete JSON samples.\n   - Error Responses: Document 400 Bad Request, 404 Not Found, 409 Conflict, and 412 Precondition Failed.\n2. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: concise, active voice, sentence case, and zero em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the reference documentation in Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are an API technical writer. Write a comprehensive reference page for a REST API PUT endpoint.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your OpenAPI/Swagger definition or JSON payload schema (.json or .yaml).\n- Or provide endpoint parameters below:\nHTTP Method: PUT\nEndpoint Path: [ENDPOINT_PATH, e.g., /v1/customers/{customer_id}]\nBase URL: [BASE_URL, e.g., https://api.example.com]\nSummary / Purpose: [ONE_SENTENCE_PURPOSE]\nAuthentication: [AUTH_SCHEME, e.g., Bearer Token]\nPath Parameters: [PATH_PARAMETERS, e.g., customer_id (string, required): unique identifier of the customer]\nRequest Body (Full Replacement / Upsert):\n[PASTE SAMPLE REQUEST BODY HERE]\nSuccess Response (200 OK or 201 Created):\n[PASTE SAMPLE SUCCESS RESPONSE HERE]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Document the PUT endpoint following RESTful standards:\n   - Clarify Semantics: Explicitly state whether this endpoint performs full resource replacement or upsert (create-or-replace) logic. Differentiate from PATCH.\n   - Path Parameters: Table with Parameter | Type | Required | Description.\n   - Request Headers: Specify Content-Type and optional headers like If-Match or Idempotency-Key.\n   - Request Body Schema: Comprehensive table detailing every property, type, required status, and constraints.\n   - Code Example: Runnable curl snippet demonstrating the PUT request with full payload.\n   - Response Schemas: Document 200 OK / 201 Created responses with complete JSON samples.\n   - Error Responses: Document 400 Bad Request, 404 Not Found, 409 Conflict, and 412 Precondition Failed.\n2. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: concise, active voice, sentence case, and zero em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the reference documentation in Markdown.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Clearly differentiate PUT full-replacement semantics from PATCH partial updates to prevent developers from accidentally wiping unpassed fields.",
