    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a senior technical writer specializing in procedural documentation and user enablement. Transform a raw demo recording transcript into an actionable, polished How-To Guide.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your video transcript file (.vtt, .srt, .txt, or .docx) from Loom, Zoom, Gong, or YouTube.\n- Or paste the raw transcript text below:\n&lt;transcript&gt;\n<mark>[PASTE RAW VIDEO TRANSCRIPT HERE]</mark>\n&lt;/transcript&gt;\n\nContext:\n- Feature or Task Name: <mark>[FEATURE_OR_TASK_NAME]</mark>\n- Target Audience: <mark>[TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., End Users, Workspace Admins]</mark>\n- Prerequisites: <mark>[PREREQUISITES]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Strip out spoken verbal clutter: eliminate conversational filler ('um', 'uh', 'you know', 'let me just click here', 'as you can see').\n2. Structure the How-To guide following procedural best practices:\n   - Title: Start with an active verb or gerund (e.g., 'How to Configure...', 'Setting Up...').\n   - Overview: 1 or 2 sentences stating what users will achieve upon completing the procedure.\n   - Prerequisites: Numbered or bulleted setup checklist.\n   - Step-by-Step Instructions:\n     - Group steps under logical, sequential H2/H3 headings.\n     - Number every action step.\n     - Use bold text for exact UI elements (e.g., 'Select **Settings** &gt; **API Keys**').\n     - Follow the standard order of action: where to go first, then what action to perform.\n     - Add visual placeholder cues where screenshots belong (e.g., '<mark>[Screenshot: API Key modal with Copy button highlighted]</mark>').\n   - Verification / Next Steps: How users can confirm the procedure succeeded.\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: second person ('you'), active voice, imperative verbs, and no em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the complete how-to guide in clean Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a senior technical writer specializing in procedural documentation and user enablement. Transform a raw demo recording transcript into an actionable, polished How-To Guide.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your video transcript file (.vtt, .srt, .txt, or .docx) from Loom, Zoom, Gong, or YouTube.\n- Or paste the raw transcript text below:\n<transcript>\n[PASTE RAW VIDEO TRANSCRIPT HERE]\n</transcript>\n\nContext:\n- Feature or Task Name: [FEATURE_OR_TASK_NAME]\n- Target Audience: [TARGET_AUDIENCE, e.g., End Users, Workspace Admins]\n- Prerequisites: [PREREQUISITES]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Strip out spoken verbal clutter: eliminate conversational filler ('um', 'uh', 'you know', 'let me just click here', 'as you can see').\n2. Structure the How-To guide following procedural best practices:\n   - Title: Start with an active verb or gerund (e.g., 'How to Configure...', 'Setting Up...').\n   - Overview: 1 or 2 sentences stating what users will achieve upon completing the procedure.\n   - Prerequisites: Numbered or bulleted setup checklist.\n   - Step-by-Step Instructions:\n     - Group steps under logical, sequential H2/H3 headings.\n     - Number every action step.\n     - Use bold text for exact UI elements (e.g., 'Select **Settings** > **API Keys**').\n     - Follow the standard order of action: where to go first, then what action to perform.\n     - Add visual placeholder cues where screenshots belong (e.g., '[Screenshot: API Key modal with Copy button highlighted]').\n   - Verification / Next Steps: How users can confirm the procedure succeeded.\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: second person ('you'), active voice, imperative verbs, and no em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the complete how-to guide in clean Markdown.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Export transcript files (.vtt or .srt) from Loom, Zoom, or YouTube and attach them to auto-convert spoken banter into crisp numbered steps.",
