    "id": "p45",
    "number": "45",
    "categoryId": "apidocs",
    "categoryName": "Sample Product Documentation Prompts",
    "title": "Generate UI Screenshot Alt Text",
    "useCase": "Write descriptive, accessible alt text for software screenshots and diagrams",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "badgeColor": "#0d9488",
    "promptText": "You are a digital accessibility (a11y) specialist and technical writer. Generate compliant, descriptive alternative text (alt text) and extended descriptions for software screenshots or architecture diagrams.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached image or UI screenshot (recommended):\n- Attach your image file (.png, .jpg, .svg, or .webp).\n- Or describe the image and UI context below:\nUI Element / Screenshot Context: <mark>[DESCRIBE THE SCREENSHOT, e.g., User permissions dashboard showing role dropdown and invite button]</mark>\nDocumentation Topic: <mark>[DOC_TOPIC, e.g., Inviting new team members to an enterprise workspace]</mark>\nKey Information the Reader Must Glean: <mark>[KEY_TAKEAWAY, e.g., Location of the Role dropdown menu]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Review the attached image or screenshot description.\n2. Provide three accessibility assets:\n   - Inline Alt Text (under 125 characters): Concise, functional description capturing the core action or state without redundant phrases like 'image of' or 'screenshot showing'.\n   - Detailed Caption (1 to 2 sentences): Contextual description placed below the image in the doc to support all visual readers.\n   - Long Description / Accessible Table (for complex UI, charts, or diagrams): Structured Markdown or list providing complete textual equivalence for screen reader users (WCAG 2.2 Level AA compliance).\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Accessibility and Writing Style Guidelines: clear, objective, sentence case, and zero em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput the three accessibility assets with Markdown embedding examples:\n- `!<mark>[Inline alt text]</mark>(screenshot.png)`\n- Caption snippet\n- Extended accessible description block\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a digital accessibility (a11y) specialist and technical writer. Generate compliant, descriptive alternative text (alt text) and extended descriptions for software screenshots or architecture diagrams.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached image or UI screenshot (recommended):\n- Attach your image file (.png, .jpg, .svg, or .webp).\n- Or describe the image and UI context below:\nUI Element / Screenshot Context: [DESCRIBE THE SCREENSHOT, e.g., User permissions dashboard showing role dropdown and invite button]\nDocumentation Topic: [DOC_TOPIC, e.g., Inviting new team members to an enterprise workspace]\nKey Information the Reader Must Glean: [KEY_TAKEAWAY, e.g., Location of the Role dropdown menu]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Review the attached image or screenshot description.\n2. Provide three accessibility assets:\n   - Inline Alt Text (under 125 characters): Concise, functional description capturing the core action or state without redundant phrases like 'image of' or 'screenshot showing'.\n   - Detailed Caption (1 to 2 sentences): Contextual description placed below the image in the doc to support all visual readers.\n   - Long Description / Accessible Table (for complex UI, charts, or diagrams): Structured Markdown or list providing complete textual equivalence for screen reader users (WCAG 2.2 Level AA compliance).\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Accessibility and Writing Style Guidelines: clear, objective, sentence case, and zero em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput the three accessibility assets with Markdown embedding examples:\n- `![Inline alt text](screenshot.png)`\n- Caption snippet\n- Extended accessible description block\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Attach your UI screenshot or diagram image directly so the model can inspect exact button labels, menus, and visual hierarchies.",
    "tags": [
      "screenshot",
      "text",
      "alt",
      "generate"
    ],
    "domain": "tech",
    "domainName": "Technical Writing",
    "subcategoryId": "draft_content",
