    "categoryName": "General Writing",
    "title": "Craft a Compelling Professional Bio (3 Lengths)",
    "useCase": "Generate 50-word, 100-word, and 200-word bios for LinkedIn, speaker pages, or portfolios",
    "level": "Beginner",
    "badgeColor": "#3b82f6",
    "promptText": "You are a personal branding strategist and executive publicist. Craft a versatile, engaging professional bio in three standard industry lengths.\n\n&lt;input_sources&gt;\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your resume, CV, or portfolio summary (.pdf, .docx, or .md).\n- Or provide your background details below:\nFull Name: <mark>[FULL_NAME]</mark>\nCurrent Title / Specialization: <mark>[TITLE_OR_SPECIALIZATION, e.g., Staff API Technical Writer and Information Architect]</mark>\nYears of Experience &amp; Key Domains: <mark>[EXPERIENCE, e.g., 8 years in cloud infrastructure, developer documentation, and developer relations]</mark>\nMajor Achievements or Notable Companies: <mark>[NOTABLE_WINS_OR_BRANDS]</mark>\nPassions / Hobbies / Personal Flavour (optional): <mark>[PERSONAL_INTERESTS, e.g., Mechanical keyboards, open-source contributor, marathon runner]</mark>\nTarget Audience: <mark>[AUDIENCE, e.g., Conference attendees, executive hiring managers, newsletter readers]</mark>\n&lt;/input_sources&gt;\n\n&lt;instructions&gt;\n1. Generate three distinct, polished bio lengths in both Third-Person and First-Person perspectives:\n   - Micro Bio (~50 words): Snappy, memorable summary ideal for speaker cards, social bios, or podcast intros.\n   - Medium Bio (~100 words): Balanced overview highlighting expertise, track record, and current mission, ideal for LinkedIn summaries or author bylines.\n   - Long Bio (~200 words): Narrative profile covering career journey, major innovations, philosophy, and personal touch, ideal for personal websites or conference programs.\n2. For each length, provide the exact word count.\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: active voice, authentic tone, and zero em-dashes.\n&lt;/instructions&gt;\n\n&lt;output_format&gt;\nOutput all three bio lengths (Third-Person and First-Person versions) with word counts in clean Markdown.\n&lt;/output_format&gt;",
    "copyPrompt": "You are a personal branding strategist and executive publicist. Craft a versatile, engaging professional bio in three standard industry lengths.\n\n<input_sources>\nAttached documents (recommended):\n- Attach your resume, CV, or portfolio summary (.pdf, .docx, or .md).\n- Or provide your background details below:\nFull Name: [FULL_NAME]\nCurrent Title / Specialization: [TITLE_OR_SPECIALIZATION, e.g., Staff API Technical Writer and Information Architect]\nYears of Experience & Key Domains: [EXPERIENCE, e.g., 8 years in cloud infrastructure, developer documentation, and developer relations]\nMajor Achievements or Notable Companies: [NOTABLE_WINS_OR_BRANDS]\nPassions / Hobbies / Personal Flavour (optional): [PERSONAL_INTERESTS, e.g., Mechanical keyboards, open-source contributor, marathon runner]\nTarget Audience: [AUDIENCE, e.g., Conference attendees, executive hiring managers, newsletter readers]\n</input_sources>\n\n<instructions>\n1. Generate three distinct, polished bio lengths in both Third-Person and First-Person perspectives:\n   - Micro Bio (~50 words): Snappy, memorable summary ideal for speaker cards, social bios, or podcast intros.\n   - Medium Bio (~100 words): Balanced overview highlighting expertise, track record, and current mission, ideal for LinkedIn summaries or author bylines.\n   - Long Bio (~200 words): Narrative profile covering career journey, major innovations, philosophy, and personal touch, ideal for personal websites or conference programs.\n2. For each length, provide the exact word count.\n3. Adhere to Microsoft Writing Style Guide: active voice, authentic tone, and zero em-dashes.\n</instructions>\n\n<output_format>\nOutput all three bio lengths (Third-Person and First-Person versions) with word counts in clean Markdown.\n</output_format>",
    "proTip": "Include an authentic personal interest or hobby to give your bio genuine human warmth alongside your technical credentials.",
